      ":question/id": "1f1b6fe2-6a21-5d73-a166-b747084826d1",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-z &=15 \\\\ y-z &=10 \\\\ z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that $z=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(5)=10\\,⟹\\,y=10-(-5)=15.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $y=15$ and $z=5$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(15)-(5)=15\\,⟹\\,x=15-(-15)-(-5)=35.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=35$, $y=15$, and $z=5.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨35,15,5⟩.$",
