      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=14 \\\\ {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3} &=21 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=- \\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{7}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6(- \\frac{7}{3})=21\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=21-(14)=7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=7$ and ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{7}{3}$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(7)-(- \\frac{7}{3})=14\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=14-(7)-(\\frac{7}{3})=\\frac{14}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{14}{3}$, ${x}_{2}=7$, and ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{7}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{14}{3} \\\\ 7 \\\\ - \\frac{7}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.$",
